## Verification

Discover the project's narrowest relevant check and full gate. Run focused
checks during work and the full gate before completion. Never weaken a gate.
Never cite volatile evidence (`tmp/`, `.agent/`, logs, `*.ndjson` ledgers) by line, count, or excerpt in a committed file.
Never re-point a drifted citation or re-record one run's timing in a budget fact; replace the check's oracle instead.
If verification cannot finish, keep diagnosing or repairing it. The rule on when a partial result is
permitted lives in `shared/_no_exemption_for_failures.j2` — refer to it
before reporting a partial.
{% if SKILL_INSTALLED_VERIFICATION_BEFORE_COMPLETION|default('') == "true" %}
Use verification-before-completion before claiming work is complete or submitting results, so the result carries fresh evidence.
{% else %}
Run fresh verification commands before claiming work is complete or submitting results, so the result carries fresh evidence.
{% endif %}
